Date: Tue, 16 Mar 93 18:57:04 CST
From: twb3@midway.uchicago.edu (Tom Morrow)
Subject: META: Is an armed society a polite society?

I argued that lurkers will not find the loss of posting privileges to be
much of a threat, and that Robin's "Polite Society" would thus have to curb
reading rights, too.  Robin replied:

>For a net-wide society, its much harder to imagine monitoring the loss
>of all reading abilities.  And I'm reluctant to have rules that can't
>be enforced.  Do you still advocate losing reading rights for a
>net-wide society?

Well, not unless you think a "no reading" rule could be enforced on the
merit system.  I agree, after all, that it is virtually impossible (ha ha)
to enforce such a rule on a net-wide basis.  It's hard to enforce such a
rule even for one list.  

I thus conclude that there is an imbalance in the Polite Society's payoff
scheme.  Everybody gets the right to shoot.  But only some of the Society's
members face significant costs from being shot--namely, those who post a
lot.  

I picture it this way:  the Polite Society is like a shootout on the
mainstreet of a frontier town.  Some gunslingers are out in the open,
talking a mile-a-minute and sometimes saying things that insult
thin-skinned listeners.  Other gunslingers--assassins, really--are
listening from the safety of windows and rooftops.  When they don't like
something they hear, they pop off a shot and take down the offender.  Sure,
folks can fire back at the assassins, but as in western movies, these
bullets don't really do much harm.

I am the sort of guy who likes to walk down the middle of the street and
talk loud, and I don't tend to take offense when others' spout off
gibberish.  I just tune them out.  So while I admire Robin's ingenuity, it
just wouldn't be smart for me to join the Polite Society.  Especially when
it looks like I'm headed for an ambush!  Tim May writes:

>Having been . . . chastened by Tom
>Morrow's argument that I have engaged in "sloppy reasoning" (a worse insult
>to me than calling me a Druid!) . . .

(*Gulp*!  No offense intended!  You aren't going to issue a decision
finding me epistemologically lacking, are you?  8-) 

>I have decided to temporarily set aside my concerns and join "The Polite >Society." . . .
>Let's get some other targets--er, I mean, "members." Kicking Robin off the
>list for a month won't be much fun. Tom? 

As Wayne and Garth would say:  "Sheeeeeeeeright!"

Expect to see me in "Polite Town", though.  I'll be the wrangler armed with
only my wits and protected by a bullet-proof vest.  Yee Haw!

