If you observed this happening in realspace, it would indicate that the
source of the images was projected light, rather than pigments that reflect
light.  When you mix primary pigments (cyan, magenta, yellow) you get
black.  When you mix lights in the primaries (blue, red, green), you get
white. 

To speak loosely, this suggests that you were watching slides, rather than
looking at paintings.


